## Why This Is Asked

Examines practical concurrency design for ordering guarantees under backpressure in a multi-client, multi-document setting, including missing/late edits and dynamic scaling.

## Key Concepts

- Bounded queues and backpressure signaling
- Per-document causal ordering using logical clocks or vector clocks
- Per-document buffers and a scheduler that avoids cross-document reordering
- Dynamic worker scaling and fault-tolerant enqueue/consume paths

## Code Example

```javascript
// Skeleton enqueue/consume sketch for per-document causal ordering
class DocBuffer {
  constructor() {
    this.frontier = new Map(); // docId -> lastCommittedClock
    this.buffers  = new Map(); // docId -> priority queue of edits
  }
  enqueue(edit) {
    const { document_id } = edit;
    if (!this.buffers.has(document_id)) this.buffers.set(document_id, []);
    // insert into per-doc heap with key = edit.clock
  }
  tryCommit(document_id) {
    // commit edits in order if their clocks are contiguous with frontier
  }
}
```

